    <bpmn:process id="W_W1313" name="W1313. Vendor-Supplied Merchandising Fixture, Display &amp; Point-of-Purchase (POP) Material Lifecycle Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor offers merchandising fixture/display for new product launch; or seasonal display refresh; or existing vendor display requires replacement/repair
Frequency: ~50–80 new vendor displays deployed chain-wide per month; ~20–30 existing displays repaired/replaced per month
Volume: ~500–800 active vendor displays across 200 stores at any time; ~840–1,300 display lifecycle events per year (per the monthly Frequency)
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Visual Merchandising Coordinator, Store Manager, Department Supervisor, Vendor Account Manager, Facilities Coordinator
Source: workflow W1313 — Vendor-Supplied Merchandising Fixture, Display &amp; Point-of-Purchase (POP) Material Lifecycle Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1313_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1313_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1313_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1313_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1313_Start4" name="Vendor offers merchandising fixture/display for new product launch; or seasonal display…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1313_Task5" name="Display request &amp; vendor agreement review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Display request &amp; vendor agreement review: (a) Vendor Account Manager submits display proposal: (i) display type (wall unit, end-cap, island, counter-top, demo station), (ii) dimensions and space requirements, (iii) products featured, (iv) proposed store placement (planogram location), (v) display duration, (vi) exclusivity requirements, (vii) cost allocation (vendor-funded, co-op funded, or BuildRight-funded), (viii) assembly and installation requirements; (b) Category Manager reviews: (i) does the display align with BuildRight&#x27;s planogram and category strategy?, (ii) does the display conflict with other vendor displays?, (iii) is the space allocation reasonable (not displacing higher-margin products without justification)?, (iv) is the vendor&#x27;s sales volume sufficient to justify the display space?; (c) Visual Merchandising Coordinator reviews for: (i) visual standards compliance (consistent with BuildRight store aesthetic), (ii) safety (stable, no tip-over risk, no sharp edges, no electrical hazards for lighted displays), (iii) ADA/PWD accessibility (not blocking aisles per W497); (d) Category Manager approves or requests modifications
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Visual Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours per display proposal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1313_Task6" name="Display deployment &amp; installation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Display deployment &amp; installation: (a) for chain-wide deployments (all 200 stores): (i) vendor ships display components to DC for distribution, (ii) DC consolidates with store replenishment shipments per W4, (iii) Department Supervisor receives and stages display components per planogram instruction sheet, (iv) for complex displays (power tool demo station, lighted appliance wall): vendor sends installation team or BuildRight Facilities Coordinator installs per vendor instructions, (v) for simple displays (counter-top, signage, bin display): Department Supervisor assembles and places per planogram; (b) system records display deployment: (i) display ID, vendor, store, location, products featured, installation date, display duration, removal date, (ii) display items tagged in planogram module for planogram compliance checking per W69; (c) photo documentation: Department Supervisor photographs installed display and uploads to ERP for vendor verification and Visual Merchandising audit
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per store: 30 min (simple) to 4 hours (complex)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1313_Task7" name="Display maintenance &amp; condition monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Display maintenance &amp; condition monitoring: (a) Department Supervisor monitors display condition during daily walkthrough (W5A): (i) physical condition: clean, no damage, all lights working (for lighted displays), all product facings stocked, signage current; (b) if display requires maintenance: (i) minor (replace light bulb, clean, restock product): Department Supervisor handles immediately, (ii) major (structural damage, electrical failure, missing components): Maintenance/Utility Staff creates work order per W47, vendor contacted for replacement parts; (c) monthly: Visual Merchandising Coordinator conducts display condition audit per store (rotating — each store audited at least once per quarter): (i) display present and in agreed location?, (ii) display in good condition?, (iii) products correctly stocked per display planogram?, (iv) competing brands not within exclusivity zone?, (v) photo audit uploaded to ERP
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Visual Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Weekly: 5 min/display; Monthly audit: 15 min/display</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1313_Task8" name="Display refresh &amp; seasonal rotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Display refresh &amp; seasonal rotation: (a) for seasonal displays: at seasonal transition per W1257: (i) remove previous season&#x27;s vendor display (e.g., summer garden display), (ii) install new season&#x27;s vendor display (e.g., rainy season waterproofing display), (iii) return previous display components to vendor via DC backhaul or dispose per vendor agreement; (b) for product launch displays: (i) after launch period (typically 4–8 weeks): convert to standard shelf display or remove if product not adopted into regular assortment, (ii) if product is adopted: replace promotional display with permanent shelf presence; (c) vendor pays for display refresh costs (new signage, updated graphics) per agreement
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Visual Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per refresh: 30 min – 2 hours per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1313_Task9" name="Display removal &amp; space recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Display removal &amp; space recovery: (a) at display agreement expiration: (i) Department Supervisor removes display and restores selling space to standard planogram, (ii) display components: return to vendor (high-value fixtures), recycle (cardboard/pop materials), or dispose (damaged items) per agreement, (iii) system removes display from planogram and records removal date; (b) if display was vendor-owned: verify return condition meets vendor&#x27;s requirements (no excessive damage beyond normal wear); (c) Category Manager evaluates display performance: (i) sales uplift during display period vs. pre-display period, (ii) display ROI: incremental sales × margin vs. display space opportunity cost, (iii) recommend to vendor: renew, modify, or discontinue display arrangement
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per removal: 15–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1313_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1313_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1313_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1313_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1313_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1313_Annotation11" targetRef="W1313_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow13" sourceRef="W1313_Start4" targetRef="W1313_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow14" sourceRef="W1313_Task5" targetRef="W1313_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow15" sourceRef="W1313_Task6" targetRef="W1313_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow16" sourceRef="W1313_Task7" targetRef="W1313_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow17" sourceRef="W1313_Task8" targetRef="W1313_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1313_Flow18" sourceRef="W1313_Task9" targetRef="W1313_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1313_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1313_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1313">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1313_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1313_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
