    <bpmn:process id="W_W1345" name="W1345. Product Barcode &amp; Label Accuracy Verification, GS1 Compliance &amp; Print Quality Audit" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New SKU onboarding (W1); vendor-supplied barcode quality complaint from POS scan failures; periodic GS1 compliance audit; or label printer maintenance cycle
Frequency: Per new SKU (~2,000–2,500/year); quarterly compliance audit across 200 stores; ad-hoc for scan failure investigation
Volume: ~2,000–2,500 new SKUs/year requiring barcode verification; ~35,000 active SKUs with shelf labels; 200 stores × ~175 shelf label changes/store/month
Owner: Content Manager
Participants: Content Specialist, Category Manager, Store Department Supervisor, IT POS System Administrator, Vendor (barcode source), GS1 Philippines
Source: workflow W1345 — Product Barcode &amp; Label Accuracy Verification, GS1 Compliance &amp; Print Quality Audit</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1345_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1345_Lane1" name="Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1345_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1345_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1345_Lane4" name="IT POS System Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1345_Lane5" name="Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1345_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1345_Start7" name="New SKU onboarding (W1); vendor-supplied barcode quality complaint from POS scan…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1345_Task8" name="Barcode verification for new SKUs">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Barcode verification for new SKUs: During new SKU onboarding per W1: (a) Content Specialist receives product sample with vendor-applied barcode from Category Manager, (b) scan barcode using POS scanner — verify: (i) barcode scans successfully on first attempt, (ii) scanned number matches item master GTIN/EAN in ERP, (iii) product description on scan matches physical item, (c) if barcode does not scan: (i) check barcode type (EAN-13, UPC-A, QR code — POS must support all), (ii) check print quality: bar width, contrast, quiet zone (minimum 5mm on each side), (iii) if vendor barcode is defective: request replacement barcode label from vendor or assign BuildRight internal barcode, (d) for BuildRight private-label items: Content Specialist assigns GS1 barcode from BuildRight&#x27;s GS1 Philippines prefix; register in GS1 Philippines GEPIR (Global Electronic Party Information Register)
Responsible (R): Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 5 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1345_Task9" name="Shelf label generation &amp; accuracy">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Shelf label generation &amp; accuracy: (a) system auto-generates shelf labels from item master per W63 when: new SKU created, price change processed per W14, or planogram reset deployed per W86, (b) Content Manager configures label template: product description, price (current retail), unit of measure, barcode (shelf label barcode = item GTIN for scan-to-verify at POS), BuildRight logo, (c) for promotional labels per W13: include promotional price, original price, promotional period, (d) system validates label content against item master before print: description match, price match, barcode match — any discrepancy blocks label printing
Responsible (R): System / Content Manager
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min/template update</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1345_Task10" name="In-store label print quality audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: In-store label print quality audit: Quarterly, Department Supervisor verifies shelf labels in assigned categories during store walkthrough per W5A: (a) sample 50 shelf labels per department: (i) does the price on shelf label match POS scan price? (scan label barcode at POS to verify), (ii) is the product description correct and current?, (iii) is the label clean, legible, and properly positioned in label holder?, (iv) is the label for the correct product (not a mislabeled shelf position)?, (b) report discrepancies to Store Manager: (i) price mismatch: update immediately — DTI compliance risk per RA 7394, (ii) description error: request label reprint via store operations app, (iii) missing label: generate and print replacement, (c) Store Manager tracks label accuracy rate per department — target &gt; 99%
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 60 min/store/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1345_Task11" name="POS scan failure tracking &amp; vendor feedback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: POS scan failure tracking &amp; vendor feedback: (a) POS system logs scan failures: barcode that required manual entry, failed scan requiring rescan, or cashier override per W5B, (b) IT POS System Administrator compiles monthly scan failure report by SKU: (i) SKUs with &gt; 5 scan failures/month flagged for barcode investigation, (ii) common failure causes: damaged barcode (in-transit damage), poor print quality (vendor issue), incorrect barcode type, (c) for vendor-caused barcode failures: Category Manager contacts vendor to: (i) provide barcode quality specifications, (ii) request barcode correction in next shipment, (iii) for chronic failures: require vendor to submit barcode sample for pre-approval before production, (d) for in-transit damage: review receiving and stock handling per W3 to identify damage points
Responsible (R): IT POS System Administrator / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1345_Task12" name="GS1 Philippines compliance &amp; membership">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: GS1 Philippines compliance &amp; membership: (a) Content Manager maintains BuildRight&#x27;s GS1 Philippines membership: annual renewal, company prefix management, (b) for BuildRight private-label items (estimated 500–800 SKUs): (i) assign GTIN from BuildRight&#x27;s GS1 prefix per GS1 rules (unique GTIN per product variant), (ii) register product data in GS1 Philippines data pool (per GDSN — Global Data Synchronization Network standards if applicable), (iii) ensure GTIN assignment follows GS1 rules: new GTIN required for product changes (size change, formulation change, packaging change), (c) annual: Content Manager verifies all BuildRight GTINs are properly registered and no duplicates exist
Responsible (R): Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 5 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1345_Task13" name="Label printer maintenance &amp; supplies">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Label printer maintenance &amp; supplies: (a) each store has 1–2 barcode label printers (thermal transfer) for shelf labels and receiving labels, (b) quarterly: Department Supervisor tests label printer: print quality check (barcode scan test), ribbon and label stock levels, cleaning cycle, (c) IT provides printer maintenance per W265 and supplies reorder process, (d) annual: IT evaluates printer fleet for replacement based on age, failure rate, and print quality
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / IT
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Quarterly check: 15 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1345_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1345_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1345_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1345_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: quarterly label audits and system-enforced price validation; operational: barcode verification at SKU onboarding; operational: batch-printing labels by aisle and recycling old labels
Owner: Content Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1345_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1345_Annotation15" targetRef="W1345_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
