    <bpmn:process id="W_W1346" name="W1346. Multilingual Product Content Localization (Filipino/English) &amp; Regional Variant Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New SKU content creation (W50); quarterly content localization audit; customer feedback requesting Filipino-language content; or regional product variant launch
Frequency: Per new SKU (~2,000–2,500/year); quarterly localization quality audit; annual regional variant review
Volume: ~35,000 active SKUs requiring bilingual content (Filipino and English); ~5–10 regional variants per category; ecommerce site and mobile app serving bilingual content
Owner: Content Manager
Participants: Content Specialist (Filipino), Category Manager, Ecommerce Manager, Marketing (brand voice), Store Operations (regional variant input)
Source: workflow W1346 — Multilingual Product Content Localization (Filipino/English) &amp; Regional Variant Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1346_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1346_Lane1" name="Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1346_Lane2" name="Ecommerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1346_Lane3" name="Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1346_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1346_Start5" name="New SKU content creation (W50); quarterly content localization audit; customer feedback…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task6" name="Bilingual content creation for new SKUs">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bilingual content creation for new SKUs: During PIM enrichment per W50: (a) Content Specialist creates English product content: description, features, specifications, application instructions, (b) Content Specialist (Filipino) creates Filipino equivalent: (i) translate short description (50–100 chars) for search results, (ii) translate long description (200–500 chars) for product page — not literal translation but localization for Filipino consumer understanding (e.g., &quot;threaded galvanized pipe&quot; → &quot;tubong galvanize na may rosas&quot; — using common Filipino construction terminology), (iii) translate key features and benefits in natural Filipino, (iv) add Filipino search keywords and synonyms (e.g., &quot;mento&quot; for cement, &quot;tubo&quot; for pipe, &quot;kable&quot; for wire), (c) for technical specifications: retain in both English and Filipino where relevant (e.g., &quot;thickness: 10mm / kapal: 10mm&quot;), (d) system stores both language versions in PIM per SKU
Responsible (R): Content Specialist / Content Specialist (Filipino)
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 10 min/SKU additional</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task7" name="Regional naming variant management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Regional naming variant management: Content Specialist manages regional product name variants: (a) compile regional naming database from: (i) Store Manager input (what do customers in their area call products?), (ii) POS search log analysis (what search terms do customers use in different regions?), (iii) Category Manager regional market knowledge, (b) for each SKU: store primary name (English), Filipino name, and up to 3 regional variants: (i) e.g., PVC pipe: English &quot;PVC pipe,&quot; Filipino &quot;tubong PVC,&quot; Cebuano &quot;tubo nga PVC,&quot; Ilocano &quot;paltog a PVC,&quot; (c) regional variants indexed for in-store kiosk search, ecommerce search, and mobile app search — customer searching in regional language finds the correct product, (d) quarterly: review regional search analytics — new search terms not matching existing SKUs indicate missing regional variants
Responsible (R): Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5 min/SKU; 4 hours/quarter for variant review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task8" name="Ecommerce &amp; app bilingual deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ecommerce &amp; app bilingual deployment: (a) ecommerce platform displays product content in user&#x27;s language preference (Filipino or English, selectable via toggle or browser locale), (b) mobile app language follows device language setting (Filipino if device is set to Filipino), (c) search engine supports both languages: customer searching &quot;pintura&quot; (Filipino) or &quot;paint&quot; (English) gets same results, (d) product recommendations per W200 served in customer&#x27;s preferred language, (e) email and push notification content per W300 sent in customer&#x27;s language preference from CRM profile
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / IT
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: Per deployment; maintenance ~4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task9" name="In-store bilingual signage &amp; shelf labels">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: In-store bilingual signage &amp; shelf labels: (a) shelf labels per W63 display product name in both languages where applicable: English primary name + Filipino name in smaller text below, (b) category signage (aisle markers, department headers) bilingual: &quot;Electrical / Kuryente,&quot; &quot;Plumbing / Tubo,&quot; &quot;Paint / Pintura,&quot; (c) promotional signage per W13 bilingual for consumer-facing materials, (d) store associate training materials per W51 available in both languages
Responsible (R): Content Manager / Visual Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per signage update cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task10" name="Quarterly localization quality audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly localization quality audit: Content Manager conducts quarterly quality audit: (a) sample 100 SKUs: verify Filipino descriptions are accurate, natural, and helpful (not machine-translated gibberish), (b) check ecommerce site: are Filipino toggle and search working correctly?, (c) review customer feedback: are customers complaining about unclear product descriptions?, (d) check regional variant coverage: which regions have the most missing variants?, (e) prioritize content improvement backlog based on audit findings
Responsible (R): Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1346_Task11" name="Translation vendor management (if outsourced)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Translation vendor management (if outsourced): If BuildRight outsources Filipino translation to external agency: (a) Content Manager manages translation vendor: SLA (48-hour turnaround per batch of 50 SKUs), quality standards (native Filipino speaker with construction/hardware vocabulary), glossary of standard terms (maintained by Content Manager), (b) quarterly vendor performance review: accuracy, timeliness, cost per SKU, (c) maintain internal glossary of BuildRight-specific Filipino terminology for consistency
Responsible (R): Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1346_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1346_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1346_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1346_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: using the most widely understood term and adding regional variants; operational: prioritizing A/B items for full Filipino localization and C-items for keyword-only; operational: using native Filipino-speaking Content Specialists or specialized translation vendors
Owner: Content Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1346_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1346_Annotation13" targetRef="W1346_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
