    <bpmn:process id="W_W1347" name="W1347. Product Recall Communication, Customer Notification &amp; Affected Inventory Quarantine" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product safety recall notice from vendor or manufacturer; DTI/BPS (Bureau of Philippine Standards) mandatory recall order; internal quality investigation identifying safety defect; or customer injury report per W140 linked to product defect
Frequency: Estimated 3–5 product recall events per year; each recall affects 1–200 stores depending on distribution
Volume: ~3–5 recalls/year affecting an estimated 50–500 SKUs total; each recall may involve thousands of units sold to customers requiring notification
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: VP Legal, COO, VP Marketing, Store Manager, LP Manager, Sustainability Lead, Customer Service Manager, Vendor Account Manager, BPS/DTI (regulatory), POS System Administrator
Source: workflow W1347 — Product Recall Communication, Customer Notification &amp; Affected Inventory Quarantine</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1347_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1347_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1347_Lane2" name="POS System Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1347_Lane3" name="VP Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1347_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1347_Lane5" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1347_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1347_Start7" name="Product safety recall notice from vendor or manufacturer; DTI/BPS (Bureau of Philippine…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task8" name="Recall trigger assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Recall trigger assessment: When a potential recall is identified: (a) VP Legal and Category Manager assess the recall trigger: (i) Vendor-initiated recall: vendor notifies BuildRight of defect — assess severity (is it a safety hazard or just quality issue?), (ii) Regulatory recall: DTI/BPS issues mandatory recall order — comply immediately, no discretion, (iii) Internal discovery: quality testing per W1 or customer complaint per W13 identifies defect — Category Manager assesses if recall is warranted, (b) classify recall severity: Class I (imminent safety hazard — fire, electrocution, structural failure risk: immediate action required), Class II (potential safety hazard: action within 48 hours), Class III (quality/performance issue — not safety-critical: action within 5 business days), (c) VP Legal determines regulatory notification requirements: DTI/BPS notification for Class I and II, (d) Category Manager identifies affected SKUs, batch/lot numbers, manufacturing dates, and distribution scope (which stores received the product)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CEO (Class I), COO (Class II–III)
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1347_Task9" name="Affected inventory quarantine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Affected inventory quarantine: (a) POS System Administrator immediately blocks affected SKUs from POS sale: system flag = &quot;Recalled — Do Not Sell&quot; (similar to W97 sample/demo block — prevents checkout scanning), (b) POS System Administrator blocks affected SKUs from ecommerce: product pages show &quot;Product temporarily unavailable&quot; or are delisted, (c) Store Manager receives recall notification via store operations app: (i) affected SKU list with batch/lot numbers, (ii) instruction: immediately remove affected products from sales floor and backroom, (iii) segregate recalled inventory: clearly label with &quot;RECALLED — DO NOT SELL&quot; tags, move to secure quarantine area, (d) Store Manager reports quarantine completion: count of affected units removed, remaining in customer hands (sold quantity minus on-hand), (e) DC Manager quarantines affected inventory at 4 DCs per same process
Responsible (R): POS System Administrator / Store Manager / DC Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours (Class I), 24–48 hours (Class II–III)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task10" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer notification: VP Marketing and Customer Service Manager execute customer notification: (a) Loyalty member notification (if affected product purchased by loyalty member per W17): (i) email notification with product image, description, hazard explanation, return instructions, and refund/exchange offer, (ii) SMS notification for Class I recalls (immediate safety hazard), (b) Trade account notification: direct phone call or email to trade customers who purchased affected product, (c) Public notification: (i) in-store recall notice posted at customer service desk and affected product aisle, (ii) website recall page with product details and return instructions, (iii) social media announcement (Facebook, the primary Philippine social platform), (iv) press release for Class I recalls, (d) Notification content: product name, SKU, batch/lot number, photo, hazard description, what to do (stop using, return to any BuildRight store), refund/exchange options, contact number for questions
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / Customer Service Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task11" name="Regulatory notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Regulatory notification: VP Legal submits required notifications: (a) DTI/BPS: for mandatory recalls — submit recall plan within 24 hours including: product identification, hazard description, distribution scope, customer notification plan, refund/exchange policy, (b) for imported products: notify Bureau of Customs if defect is in an incoming shipment, (c) maintain regulatory communication log: all submissions, responses, and compliance requirements, (d) cooperate with DTI investigation if requested: provide sales records, customer notification evidence, inventory disposition records
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task12" name="Customer return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer return processing: (a) customer returns affected product to any BuildRight store per enhanced return process: (i) Store Manager or designated supervisor handles recall returns personally (not standard cashier), (ii) no receipt required — verify product matches recall list (SKU, batch number), (iii) refund options: full cash refund, store credit, or exchange for equivalent product (customer choice), (iv) system records return as &quot;Recall Return&quot; with recall reference number (distinct from standard return per W12), (b) recalled products placed in quarantine area — not returned to stock, (c) weekly: Category Manager tracks return rate: units returned ÷ units sold — report to COO and VP Legal
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing during recall period</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task13" name="Vendor recovery &amp; disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Vendor recovery &amp; disposition: Category Manager coordinates with vendor: (a) Vendor-funded recall: vendor responsible for all costs — customer refunds, inventory value, logistics, notification expenses; Category Manager submits cost recovery claim to vendor, (b) Inventory disposition: (i) return recalled inventory to vendor (vendor provides pickup or shipping instructions), (ii) if vendor does not accept return: destroy per waste management protocol W502 with documented evidence (photos, waste manifest), (iii) for hazardous recalled products (paint, chemicals): follow hazardous waste disposal per W236, (c) Vendor accountability: for recurring recalls from same vendor, Category Manager escalates to VP Merchandising for vendor performance review per W44 and potential de-listing
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Vendor Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1347_Task14" name="Recall closure &amp; lessons learned">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Recall closure &amp; lessons learned: (a) VP Legal confirms all regulatory requirements satisfied: DTI/BPS closure confirmation, customer notification evidence, return rate documentation, (b) Category Manager compiles recall summary: units sold, units returned, return rate, total cost (refunds + logistics + notifications), vendor recovery amount, (c) COO conducts lessons-learned review: (i) was the recall response timely and effective?, (ii) what could be improved in the process?, (iii) should the vendor relationship be modified (additional quality requirements, reduced allocation)?, (d) update recall procedures if process gaps identified, (e) archive recall file for regulatory and legal records (retain 5 years per Philippine document retention requirements)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / COO / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1347_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1347_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1347_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1347_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: public notification channels (in-store, social media, press); operational: empowering POS System Administrator to execute emergency blocks without IT manager approval for safety recalls
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1347_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1347_Annotation16" targetRef="W1347_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
