    <bpmn:process id="W_W1465" name="W1465. Product Safety Data Sheet (SDS) Management, Hazmat Technical Documentation &amp; Compliance Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New SKU onboarding (W1) for chemical/hazmat products; vendor SDS update; annual SDS compliance audit; or regulatory (DENR/BPS) inquiry
Frequency: Per new chemical/hazmat SKU (~200–300/year); quarterly vendor SDS update review; annual compliance audit
Volume: ~3,500–4,200 chemical/hazmat SKUs requiring SDS (paint, thinners, solvents, adhesives, pesticides, cleaning agents); ~200–300 new SDS documents/year
Owner: Content Manager
Participants: Content Specialist, Category Manager, VP Legal (compliance), Store Department Supervisor, Vendor (SDS source), DENR/BPS (regulatory), Safety Officer
Source: workflow W1465 — Product Safety Data Sheet (SDS) Management, Hazmat Technical Documentation &amp; Compliance Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1465_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1465_Lane1" name="Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1465_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1465_Lane3" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1465_Lane4" name="Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1465_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1465_Start6" name="New SKU onboarding (W1) for chemical/hazmat products; vendor SDS update; annual SDS…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1465_Task7" name="SDS acquisition during SKU onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: SDS acquisition during SKU onboarding: During new SKU creation per W1, system checks if the item falls in a chemical/hazmat category (paint, solvent, adhesive, pesticide, cleaning agent, construction chemical, fuel). If yes: (a) Content Specialist requests SDS from vendor in GHS-compliant format (Globally Harmonized System — 16-section SDS); (b) vendor must provide SDS before the SKU can be activated for sale — system enforces &quot;SDS Required&quot; hold status; (c) Content Specialist validates SDS completeness: all 16 GHS sections present, hazard classification stated, first-aid measures included, PPE requirements specified, disposal instructions provided
Responsible (R): Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 15 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1465_Task8" name="SDS digitization &amp; storage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SDS digitization &amp; storage: (a) Content Specialist uploads vendor-provided SDS (PDF) to the PIM module linked to the SKU record per W50; (b) system extracts key metadata: hazard class, signal word (Danger/Warning), GHS pictogram codes, H-statements (hazard), P-statements (precaution), CAS numbers for chemical ingredients; (c) metadata populates item master attributes for shelf label generation per W63 and POS lookup; (d) SDS PDF accessible from store operations tablet, employee mobile app, and ecommerce product page (download link)
Responsible (R): Content Specialist / System
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 10 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1465_Task9" name="Shelf label hazard communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Shelf label hazard communication: (a) system auto-generates GHS hazard pictograms on shelf labels for chemical/hazmat SKUs per W1345 label process; (b) labels include: product name, hazard pictogram(s), signal word, primary H-statement in English and Filipino per W1346; (c) for restricted products (solvents, pesticides): POS age-restriction prompt at checkout per W5B; (d) Department Supervisor verifies shelf label hazard information during weekly walkthrough per W5A
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated + 5 min/week verification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1465_Task10" name="Employee SDS access &amp; training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Employee SDS access &amp; training: (a) store operations tablet provides instant SDS lookup by scanning product barcode or searching by name; (b) quarterly: Safety Officer conducts hazmat awareness refresher for store staff per W51 — covers SDS reading, GHS pictogram meaning, PPE requirements, spill response per W142; (c) Content Manager ensures SDS documents are available in Filipino for store-level employees per W1346 localization standards
Responsible (R): Safety Officer / Content Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Quarterly: 2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1465_Task11" name="Vendor SDS update monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Vendor SDS update monitoring: (a) quarterly: Content Specialist contacts chemical/hazmat vendors for updated SDS — manufacturers reformulate products, change suppliers, or receive new regulatory classifications; (b) system tracks SDS &quot;last updated&quot; date per SKU; (c) SDS older than 3 years flagged for vendor reconfirmation; (d) if vendor provides updated SDS: Content Specialist replaces old version, system updates hazard metadata and triggers shelf label reprint per W63 if hazard classification changed
Responsible (R): Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1465_Task12" name="Annual SDS compliance audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual SDS compliance audit: (a) Content Manager compiles SDS compliance report: (i) total chemical/hazmat SKUs vs. SKUs with current SDS on file, (ii) SDS completeness score (all 16 GHS sections populated), (iii) SDS age distribution, (iv) shelf label hazard pictogram accuracy rate; (b) VP Legal reviews compliance status for DENR and DOLE requirements; (c) any SKUs missing SDS or with outdated SDS are blocked from sale until resolved; (d) audit results reported to ESG compliance per W1330
Responsible (R): Content Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1465_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1465_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1465_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1465_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: system-enforced SDS hold at SKU onboarding
Owner: Content Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1465_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1465_Annotation14" targetRef="W1465_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1465_Flow16" sourceRef="W1465_Start6" targetRef="W1465_Task7" />
