    <bpmn:process id="W_W1466" name="W1466. Seasonal Product Content Pre-Staging, Launch Readiness Verification &amp; Cross-Channel Publishing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal buy plan finalized per W32; promotional calendar event trigger per W13; or Category Manager requests content readiness for upcoming season
Frequency: 6 major seasonal events per year (per model company seasonal calendar); each event requires ~1,000–2,000 SKUs to be content-ready
Volume: ~6,000–12,000 seasonal SKU content readiness checks per year across 6 events
Owner: Content Manager
Participants: Content Specialist, Category Manager, Ecommerce Manager, Marketing Campaign Manager, Visual Merchandising Coordinator
Source: workflow W1466 — Seasonal Product Content Pre-Staging, Launch Readiness Verification &amp; Cross-Channel Publishing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1466_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1466_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1466_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1466_Lane3" name="Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1466_Lane4" name="Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1466_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1466_Start6" name="Seasonal buy plan finalized per W32; promotional calendar event trigger per W13; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1466_Task7" name="Seasonal content intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal content intake: Category Manager finalizes seasonal buy plan per W32 and provides Content Manager with: (a) seasonal SKU list (new items, returning seasonal items, carry-over items needing content refresh), (b) season launch date (e.g., &quot;Summer 2026 — March 1&quot;), (c) target content-ready date = T-6 weeks before launch; (d) Content Manager creates seasonal content project in project tracker with SKU assignments to Content Specialists
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1466_Task8" name="Content gap analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Content gap analysis: Content Manager runs content completeness check against seasonal SKU list: (a) for each SKU, system checks: product description (Filipino and English per W1346), images (minimum 3 per SKU), attribute completeness per category schema, SDS (for chemical items per W1465), barcode/label per W1345, pricing accuracy per W14; (b) system generates gap report: &quot;Content Complete&quot; (no action), &quot;Content Partial&quot; (missing elements listed), &quot;Content Missing&quot; (no content exists — new SKU); (c) Content Manager prioritizes: new SKUs first (full content creation per W50), then partial SKUs (gap filling), then complete SKUs (verification only)
Responsible (R): System / Content Manager
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: 2 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1466_Task9" name="Content creation &amp; enrichment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Content creation &amp; enrichment: Content Specialists execute per W50 with seasonal priority: (a) new seasonal SKUs: full content creation (attributes, descriptions bilingual, images, keywords) — 45 min/SKU; (b) returning seasonal SKUs: verify content is current, update if product specifications changed, refresh lifestyle imagery if previous season&#x27;s imagery is dated — 15 min/SKU; (c) Content Manager monitors daily progress against T-6 week content-ready deadline
Responsible (R): Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Content Manager
Duration: Per W50 estimates</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1466_Task10" name="Launch readiness verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Launch readiness verification (T-2 weeks before season): Content Manager conducts formal launch readiness check: (a) 100% of seasonal SKUs have complete content (description, images, attributes, pricing) — system-enforced gate: any SKU with incomplete content is flagged and Content Specialist has 3 days to complete; (b) ecommerce category pages and seasonal landing pages built and reviewed by Ecommerce Manager; (c) marketplace listings (Shopee, Lazada) updated per W1464; (d) promotional pricing loaded in system per W13 and validated; (e) shelf label batch print files generated per W63 for distribution to stores; (f) seasonal signage and planogram updates ready per W86
Responsible (R): Content Manager / Ecommerce Manager / Marketing Campaign Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 day/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1466_Task11" name="Cross-channel synchronized publishing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cross-channel synchronized publishing (T-1 week): (a) system publishes seasonal content to ecommerce platform; (b) marketplace integration pushes updated listings to Shopee, Lazada per W180; (c) social media content (Facebook, TikTok) scheduled per W300 campaign plan; (d) shelf labels and planogram updates distributed to stores via store operations app; (e) POS product lookup and pricing updated; (f) Content Manager verifies cross-channel consistency: price, description, image, and availability match across all channels
Responsible (R): System / Content Manager / Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1466_Task12" name="Post-launch content monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-launch content monitoring: During first 2 weeks of season: (a) Content Manager monitors ecommerce product page performance: high bounce rate indicates content quality issue; (b) Customer Service reports customer complaints about product information accuracy; (c) system monitors marketplace listing errors or sync failures per W1464; (d) urgent content fixes processed within 24 hours
Responsible (R): Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/week during launch period</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1466_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1466_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1466_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1466_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-242 (ensure controlled execution — Product Information &amp; Content (PA-01.3).) | - operational: Content Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Content Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1466_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1466_Annotation14" targetRef="W1466_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
